# Phase 2: Requirement Analysis
## Functional requirements
| ID | Requirement |
|----|-------------|
| FR1 | Users can register, log in and log out |
| FR2 | Three planners: Home, Party, Jewelry |
| FR3 | Backend routes `/generate-home`, `/generate-party`, `/generate-jewelry` |
| FR4 | Gemini processes text, numbers and an optional outfit image |
| FR5 | Recommendations shown dynamically with platform, price and reason |
| FR6 | Dashboard with recent activity and full history |
| FR7 | Fallback recommendations when AI fails or exceeds budget |
## Non-functional requirements
- Responsive UI, response under ~10 s, passwords hashed, input validated, API key kept in `.env`.
## Technology stack
Python, Flask, SQLite, Google Gemini (google-genai SDK), HTML/CSS/JS.
## Constraints
Third-party platform data is mocked/simulated (no official public APIs for all sources).
